{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 138, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edges 0 (and 1) absent, edge 3 is the main input-to-output path, so removing it collapses accuracy (experiment 59)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 3 absent, edge 5 carries a key path to the output, and removing it costs far more than when edge 3 is present (experiments 63 and 39)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a skip_connect on the input edge with a 3x3 conv gains more than replacing a conv or avg_pool already doing useful work."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a missing direct edge gives a large gain, whereas replacing an existing skip_connect often does not help."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 4 with a 3x3 conv gains more than replacing an existing 1x1 conv or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty output-side edge with a 3x3 conv helps more than replacing an op that is already present."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip_connect on the intermediate edge to a 3x3 conv gives consistent gains on the harder datasets."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv from edge 1 loses learned capacity, unlike removing a weak op such as skip_connect or avg_pool."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "di